<title>MEXICO: Runaway rail car hits 14 in Mexico.</title>
<headline>Runaway rail car hits 14 in Mexico.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Some 14 people were injured on Wednesday when a runaway rail car ploughed through a railroad crossing in central Mexico hitting a truck full of workers, a local Red Cross official said.</p>
<p>Miguel Angel Gonzalez Rosales, head of the Mexican Red Cross in the central town of Tehuacan, some 130 miles (200 kms) southeast of the capital, said four of the men were seriously injured.</p>
<p>He said the rail car broke loose from a nearby factory, gathering speed as it hurtled downhill along the rail tracks, until it hit the truck.</p>
</text>
